{0 Observe Lwt Unix}

[observe-lwt-unix] is the ready Observe composition for Lwt applications on
Unix. Link it with
[(libraries observe observe-lwt-unix lwt.unix)]. Add
[(preprocess (pps observe.ppx))] when using the deriver or free-form extension.

{1 Initialization}

{[
let config =
  Observe.Config.create_exn ~service:"orders" ~environment:"development" ()

let () = Observe_lwt_unix.init_exn config

let () =
  Observe.Logs.info
    (Observe.Logs.text ~tag:"startup" "service ready")
]}

The initializer is synchronous. It installs Lwt callback-local context, the OS
wall clock, and automatic formatted output on standard error. Console records
are submitted without blocking the producer and written in order by one bounded
Lwt worker. It starts no scheduler and returns no logging handle. See
{!module:Observe_lwt_unix}.

[Config.Auto] selects pretty output for an absent, [dev], or [development]
environment and NDJSON otherwise. [Pretty], [Ndjson], and [Silent] are explicit
overrides.

Before process exit, run {!val:Observe_lwt_unix.shutdown} through the active Lwt
scheduler. Use {!val:Observe_lwt_unix.flush} when the worker should remain open.

{1 Capture}

{!val:Observe_lwt_unix.Test.with_capture} installs a bounded capture through
real Lwt callback-local state. It restores the prior route after success,
failure, or [Lwt.Canceled].
